<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stanisław Leszczyński</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1677">1677</a>–1766</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Stanisław I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Stanisław Leszczyński was a Polish noble twice made King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, first in 1704 under Swedish protection during the Great Northern War and again in 1733, when Russian and Austrian intervention in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-polish-succession">War of the Polish Succession</a> drove him out. His daughter Marie married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a>, and in 1737 he received the duchies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> and Bar for life, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneville">Lunéville</a>. On his death in 1766 they passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski.jpg" alt="Stanisław Leszczyński" width="320" height="424" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Girardet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stanislaw_Leszczynski1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
